{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The program is line-oriented with `fgets(…, 256, …)`, tokenizes only on spaces and tabs, caps tokens at 63 bytes, and keeps several fixed-capacity in-memory tables. I’ll model input as raw bytes, preserve the 255-byte `fgets` chunking and aliases/check order, and use fixed-layout byte storage where the C performs unchecked `strcpy`, so observable boundary behavior is retained without unsafe Rust memory writes."}}
